.TH TDEFLATPAK 1 "November 2026" "tdeflatpak 0.2.0" "Trinity Desktop Environment"
.SH NAME
tdeflatpak \- Flatpak manager for the Trinity Desktop Environment
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tdeflatpak
.RB [ \-\-browse | \-\-updates | \-\-search | \-\-remotes ]
.RB [ \-\-details
.IR app-id ]
.RB [ \-\-permissions
.IR app-id ]
.RI [ "generic TDE and TQt options" ]
.RI [ file ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tdeflatpak
(\(lqFlatpak Manager\(rq) is a graphical application for the Trinity Desktop
Environment (TDE) that manages Flatpak applications, runtimes and remotes.
It uses the libflatpak library directly and works on both the system-wide
installation
.RI ( /var/lib/flatpak )
and the per-user installation
.RI ( ~/.local/share/flatpak ).
.PP
The main window has five tabs:
.TP
.B Browse
An app store view of the catalog, by category. For Flathub it also shows
the Popular, Trending, New and Recently Updated lists of the Flathub web
service.
.TP
.B Installed
Lists installed applications (and optionally runtimes).
Applications can be started, their details shown and their permissions
edited; items can be uninstalled, application updates blocked and runtimes
pinned.
.TP
.B Search & Install
Searches the AppStream catalogs of all enabled remotes by name, ID or
summary, and installs the selected applications together with the runtimes
they need.
.TP
.B Updates
Checks for updates and installs all or only the selected ones.
.TP
.B Remotes
Lists remotes. Remotes can be added (from a
.I .flatpakrepo
file or URL, or Flathub with one click), enabled, disabled and removed.
Unused runtimes can be removed.
.PP
The details dialog shows the description, screenshots, releases, sizes,
download count and requested permissions of an application.
The permission editor changes what an application may access for the
current user (the same files
.B flatpak override \-\-user
writes), revokes portal permissions, deletes the application's data and
blocks its updates.
The settings and the permission editor are also available in the Trinity
Control Center
.RB ( "tdecmshell tdeflatpak\-settings" ).
.PP
Changes to the system-wide installation require authorization through
polkit, so a polkit authentication agent such as
.B polkit\-agent\-tde
must be running.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-browse
Start with the Browse tab.
.TP
.B \-\-updates
Start with the Updates tab.
.TP
.B \-\-search
Start with the Search & Install tab.
.TP
.B \-\-remotes
Start with the Remotes tab.
.TP
.BI \-\-details " app-id"
Show the details of the application
.IR app-id ,
for example
.IR org.gimp.GIMP .
.TP
.BI \-\-permissions " app-id"
Open the permission editor for the installed application
.IR app-id .
.TP
.I file
A
.I .flatpakref
file (install the application it describes) or a
.I .flatpakrepo
file (add the remote it describes). Local paths and URLs are accepted.
.PP
The generic TDE and TQt options are also supported; run
.B tdeflatpak \-\-help\-all
for the complete list.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B tdeflatpak \-\-updates
Open the Flatpak Manager and check for updates.
.TP
.B tdeflatpak \-\-permissions org.mozilla.firefox
Change what Firefox may access.
.TP
.B tdeflatpak https://dl.flathub.org/repo/flathub.flatpakrepo
Add the Flathub remote.
.TP
.B tdeflatpak org.example.App.flatpakref
Install an application from a downloaded
.I .flatpakref
file.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/lib/flatpak
System-wide Flatpak installation.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/flatpak
Per-user Flatpak installation.
.TP
.I ~/.trinity/share/config/tdeflatpakrc
Settings and window state.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/flatpak/overrides/
Per-user permission overrides
.RI ( global
applies to all applications).
.TP
.I ~/.var/app/
Per-application data.
.TP
.I ~/.trinity/cache\-*/tdeflatpak/
Cached Flathub web service responses and images.
